# Cloudflare Pages header rules. Pages consumes this file and never serves it.
#
# Why this exists (2026-07-31): returning visitors were running stale JS/CSS for
# up to four hours. New HTML plus four-hour-old code is not theoretical — it is
# what shipped after the lightbox rewrite, where the markup carried the new
# data-full hooks but the cached main.js knew nothing about them, so the
# Amenities images did not open at all.
#
# IMPORTANT — this file alone is not sufficient. The `max-age=14400` seen on the
# custom domain was NOT the Pages default: the pages.dev origin returns
# `max-age=0` for every asset. 14400 is the zone's **Browser Cache TTL**
# (Cloudflare Free plan default, 4 hours) rewriting the origin's headers. Until
# that zone setting is changed to "Respect Existing Headers"
# (Caching → Configuration → Browser Cache TTL), nothing below takes effect on
# nomadtwintowers.com. Verify with:
#   curl -sI https://nomadtwintowers.com/js/main.js | grep -i cache-control
#
# Once the zone respects origin headers, everything would otherwise inherit the
# origin's max-age=0 — including images and fonts — so the long-lived rules
# below are needed to avoid trading one problem for a slower site.

# Code: filenames are stable because there is no build step to content-hash
# them, so revalidate every load. Costs a 304 when nothing has changed.
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Renders and floor plans: new artwork ships under a new filename, so a week is
# safe. Kept revalidating after that because a few files have been overwritten
# in place (apple-touch-icon.png, the favicon rebuild on 2026-07-30).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, must-revalidate

# Self-hosted Fraunces/Manrope subsets. These genuinely never change under these
# names, so cache them hard.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
